    {
      "id": "claim_c2cb8d139e1f4f0bb979bb4c637b5d1b",
      "statement": "The OpenWiki generator's version is pinned in two places that must agree: the dev container's toolchain image installs it globally with `npm install -g openwiki@0.7.1 mermaid jsdom` (there is no repository checkout at image-build time), while the CI wiki-maintain job has no generator baked in and installs the same three exact pins from the committed lockfile in tools/openwiki-generator/ with `pnpm --dir tools/openwiki-generator install --frozen-lockfile`. tools/openwiki-generator is its own pnpm workspace root, outside the root workspace globs (frontend/*, packages/*), with a three-day minimumReleaseAge cooldown (4320 minutes, matching renovate.json's catch-all) enforced at both resolve and install time so a lockfile regeneration cannot pull in a freshly published transitive and a frozen install fails ERR_PNPM_MINIMUM_RELEASE_AGE_VIOLATION instead. scripts/__tests__/wiki-maintain.guard.test.mjs extracts the container's real install command line (skipping comment lines) against the locked manifest and fails if the versions or the mermaid/jsdom peer set differ, fails a cooldown under three days or a non-exact minimumReleaseAgeExclude entry with no matching overrides: floor, fails a root workspace glob that would swallow the generator directory, and requires the generator manifest to declare no packageManager of its own; renovate.json moves both halves in one grouped `openwiki generator` PR.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.devcontainer/toolchain.Dockerfile#L69-L86",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6013505215c5b4dff89ab4811a491999b8f1f2d228e503c82a1efbda6b6f9e4b:"
        },
